Commit two (M2 on top of Rule R) is done in the working tree, and all three lanes pass. Nothing was staged, committed or stashed. `test/yin/vm/content_test.cljc` is resolved in the file but still shows as unmerged (`UU`), as the prompt asked. The full report is at `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1790354100000-vm-engineer-yin-def-rule-r-commit-two-m2.claude-opus-5-5.report.md`.

**Conflict resolution.** I kept M2's `linker/fetch` version. The load then passes `(:contract linker/semantic-format)`, the contract of the format record the vector was fetched under, and never `vm/semantic-contract`. Passing the loader's own constant would stamp external input with it, which is the pattern codex rejected in commit one. Until the records were renamed this correctly refused v2 against v3.

